# A narrow footpath, running roughly west to east through the world origin.
#
# One `u v` pair per line, in metres. See `main_path.spline.ron` for why this is
# a line-based format rather than RON.
#
# The wander is the content. A track laid out on a straight line reads as a
# ruled edge however ragged the material boundary on top of it is, because the
# eye finds the straightness at a scale above anything the transition solver
# works at. Half a metre of drift over ten is enough to remove that without the
# path ever looking lost.
#
# It passes through the origin so that a plate centred on tile 0,0 gets the
# track across its middle with meadow on both sides.

-40   -1.2
-30   -0.6
-20    0.3
-12    0.5
 -6    0.1
 -3   -0.25
  0   -0.1
  3    0.35
  6    0.5
 12    0.15
 20   -0.5
 30   -0.3
 40    0.6
